cable; power supply differences (includes 4x 3.6V batteries; battery 6x 3.6V).\n\nCharacteristics: \n- type_level: attributes common to all — e.g., measuring principle electromagnetic, accuracy class 1 and 2, environmental class O, mechanical class M1, temperature range -25/+55 °C, water temperature class T50 (+0.1 to +50 °C), MAP 1.6 MPa, orientation all positions.\n\nBut some vary between the two groups: electromagnetic environment E2 (FEW41/43) vs E1/E2 (FEW45). Power supply differs.\n\nHmm, how to structure? I could put common attributes at type_level, and use config_level or model_level for varying ones.\n\nLet me think about the structure:\n\nType-level characteristics (common to both tables):\n- measuring_principle: \"Electromagnetic\"\n- accuracy_class: \"1 and 2\" — hmm, accuracy_classes in recommendation: [1, 2]\n- environmental_class: \"O (installed outdoors)\" → value \"O\", maybe note installed outdoors\n- mechanical_class: \"M1\"\n- temperature_range_ambient: {min: -25, max: 55} °C\n- water_temperature_class: \"T50\" with range +0.1 to +50 °C\n- maximum_admissible_pressure: 1.6 MPa\n- orientation: \"All positions\"\n- reverse_flow: sensor intended to measure reverse flow\n- checking_facilities: \"Type P (permanent) automatic checking facility\"\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_class: U0 and D0, except DN250+ → U3 and D0 — this is config-level (varies by size)\n\nModel-level (FEW45 vs FEW41/43):\n- electromagnetic_environment: E2 (FEW41/43), E1/E2 (FEW45, depending on antenna cable)\n- power supply details\n\nConfig-level:\n- pressure_loss_class varies by size (DN40/DN50, >DN50, etc.) and bore type (reduced vs full)\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_class varies by size\n\nPower supply: For Table 1: AC mains 95–240 VAC @ 50/60 Hz; renewable energy DC 6–32 V; battery 2x 3.6V (2.9-3.6V). For Table 2 (FEW45): AC mains 95-240 VAC @ 50/60 Hz including 4x 3.6V batteries; renewable 6-32 V including 4x 3.6V batteries; battery 6x 3.6V (2.9-3.6V).\n\nI'll model power_supply