ulti-part: voltage {min:95,max:240} VAC, frequency {min:50,max:60} Hz. Config values shape: {condition, value, unit_symbol}. For multi-attribute, I'd emit separate config_level entries per attribute:\n  - attribute: power_supply_voltage, axis: power_source, values: [{condition: \"AC mains\", value: {min:95, max:240}, unit_symbol: \"V\"}, ...]. Battery: 3.6 V per cell — \"2x 3.6 V\" → hmm. That's battery pack configuration. Could record power_supply_battery: {value: \"2x 3.6 V\", ...} as string with operating range. \n\nThis is getting complicated. Let me decide a pragmatic decomposition:\n\nconfig_level entries (axis: \"power source\", model_scope noted where differing):\n\n1. attribute: power_supply_voltage, axis: power_source\n   values: [{condition: \"AC mains\", value: {min:95, max:240}, unit_symbol: \"V\"}, {condition: \"renewable energy (DC powered)\", value: {min:6, max:32}, unit_symbol: \"V\"}]\n   \n   But battery count differs per model. Battery voltage per cell is 3.6 V both, count differs (2x vs 6x). So:\n   \n2. attribute: replaceable_battery_cells, axis: transmitter type\n   values: [{condition: \"FEW41Y.Z / FEW43Y.Z\", value: 2, ...}, {condition: \"FEW45Y.Z\", value: 6}]\n   unit: cells of 3.6 V. Hmm. Maybe: attribute: replaceable_battery, value string \"2x 3.6 V (operating range 2.9 – 3.6 V)\". The rules prefer structured, but strings allowed.\n\nGiven the complexity, I'll do:\n\nconfig_level:\n- {\"attribute\": \"power_supply_voltage\", \"axis\": \"power_source\", \"values\": [{\"condition\": \"AC mains\", \"value\": {\"min\": 95, \"max\": 240}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}, {\"condition\": \"renewable energy power (DC powered)\", \"value\": {\"min\": 6, \"max\": 32}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}, {\"condition\": \"replaceable battery\", \"value\": 3.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}]} — hmm battery is \"2x 3.6V\". \n\nAlternative: model the battery as:\n- attribute: replaceable_battery_configuration, axis: transmitter type\n  values: [{condition: \"FEW41Y.Z / FEW43