(varies).\n- mechanical_class: {\"value\": \"M1\"}\n- temperature_range_ambient: {\"value\": {\"min\": -25, \"max\": 55}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\n- water_temperature_class: {\"value\": \"T50\"}\n- water_temperature_range: {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 50}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\n- maximum_admissible_pressure: {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"MPa\"} — also \"(16 bar)\" parenthetical; keep just MPa.\n- orientation: {\"value\": \"All positions\"}\n- reverse_flow: {\"value\": \"The sensor is intended to measure reverse flow\"} — long. Maybe {\"value\": \"intended to measure reverse flow\"}? I'll keep original text shortened: \"sensor intended to measure reverse flow\".\n- checking_facilities: {\"value\": \"Type P (permanent) automatic checking facility\"}\n- battery_operating_range: {\"value\": {\"min\": 2.9, \"max\": 3.6}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}\n\nmodel_level:\n- electromagnetic_environment: values: [{model: \"FEW41Y.Z\", value: \"E2\"}, {model: \"FEW43Y.Z\", value: \"E2\"}, {model: \"FEW45Y.Z\", value: \"E1 or E2 (see config)\"}] — hmm messy. Alternative: type_level for FEW41/43 handled at model_level with two entries and FEW45 as config. Let me do:\n\nmodel_level: [\n  {\"attribute\": \"electromagnetic_environment\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"value\": \"E2\"}, {\"model\": \"FEW43Y.Z\", \"value\": \"E2\"}]},\n  {\"attribute\": \"power_supply_voltage\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"value\": {...}}, ...]} — no, voltage same across models; difference is battery cells and inclusion of backup batteries.\n]\n\nMaybe better: keep electromagnetic_environment at model_level with all three, where FEW45 gets config-style string \"E1 (with external antenna cable) / E2 (without)\". And ALSO add config_level entry for antenna cable axis. Redundancy is OK but noise. I'll do model_level with FEW45 value \"E1/E2 depending on antenna cable\" — plus a config_level:\n\nconfig_level:\n- {\"attribute\": \"electromagnetic_environment\", \"axis\": \"transmitter antenna cable (FEW45Y.Z)\", \"values\": [{\"condition\": \"with external antenna cable\", \"value\": \"E1\"}, {\"condition\": \"without external antenna cable\", \"value\": \"E2\"}]}\n\nAnd model_level:\n- {\"attribute\": \"electromagnetic_environment\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"value\": \"E2\"}, {\"model\": \"FEW43Y.Z\", \"value\": \"E2\"}]}\n(FEW45 covered by config.)\n\n- replaceable battery cells: model_level:\n  {\"attribute\": \"replaceable_battery_cells\", \"unit_symbol\": \"x 3.6 V\", hmm — awkward. Use value strings: {\"model\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"value\": \"2x 3.6 V\"}, {\"model\": \"FEW45Y.Z\", \"value\": \"6x 3.6 V\"}. Or numeric count with unit \"cells (3.6 V)\". I'll do:\n  {\"attribute\": \"replaceable_battery_cells\", \"unit_symbol\": \"cells\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"value\": 2}, {\"model\": \"FEW43Y.Z\", \"value\": 2}, {\"model\": \"FEW45Y.Z\", \"value\": 6}]}\n  And note battery voltage 3.6 V per cell in a type_level? add type_level battery_cell_voltage: {\"value\": 3.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}.\n\n- FEW45 backup batteries in AC/DC modes: \"including 4x 3.6 V replaceable batteries\". config_level:\n  {\"attribute\": \"backup_replaceable_battery_cells\", \"axis\": \"power_source (FEW45Y.Z)\", \"values\": [{\"condition\": \"AC mains\", \"value\": 4, \"unit_symbol\": \"cells\"}, {\"condition\": \"renewable energy power (DC powered)\", \"value\": 4, \"unit_symbol\": \"cells\"}]}\n\nHmm, this is getting heavy. Simplify: I'll capture main things and accept some string values.\n\nLet me also reconsider power supply: same for both models (95-240 VAC, 6-32 VDC). config_level axis \"power_source\":\n\n{\"attribute\": \"power_supply_voltage\", \"axis\": \"power_source\", \"values\": [\n  {\"condition\": \"AC mains\", \"value\": {\"min\": 95, \"max\": 240}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"renewable energy power (DC powered)\", \"value\": {\"min\": 6, \"max\": 32}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"replaceable battery\", \"value\": 3.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}\n]}\n\n{\"attribute\": \"power_supply_frequency\", \"axis\": \"power_source\", \"values\": [\n  {\"condition\": \"AC mains\", \"value\": {\"min\": 50, \"max\": 60}, \"unit_symbol\": \"Hz\"}\n]}\n\nOK.\n\nPressure loss config_level as above. Flow profile sensitivity config_level as above.\n\nmatrix_tables: The characteristics tables 1 and 2 are key-value tables, not multi-dim matrices. I don't think matrix_tables is needed. The schema's matrix_tables is for multi-dim tables that don't fit elsewhere. The config-level axes cover it. I'll skip matrix_tables.\n\nSoftware identification tables 3/4 — content not in this fragment (cut off at \"Table 3 Software identification for AquaMaster4 FEW41Y.Z and AquaMaster4 FEW43Y.Z variant\"). So nothing to extract.\n\nCertificate number: \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\" — should number include \"revision 12\"? Put revision in revision_history. number: \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\".\n\nNow dates: \"2 August 2021\" → 2021-08-02. \"14 August 2020\" → 2020-08-14. \"30 September 2020\" → 2020-09-30. \"24 December 2020\" → 2020-12-24. \"26 August 2021\" → 2021-08-26. \"23 November 2021\" → 2021-11-23. \"22 September 2023\" → 2023-09-22. Issue date \"7 April 2025\" → 2025-04-07.\n\nApplicant address: \"ABB Limited, Oldends Lane, GL10 3TA Stonehouse, United Kingdom\". address_lines: [\"Oldends Lane\", \"GL10 3TA Stonehouse\", \"United Kingdom\"].\n\nApplicants and manufacturers identical — per rule 12, \"Manufacturer of the certified type is the applicant\" case. The table label: \"Applicant and Manufacturer\". So both arrays get the entry.\n\nCertified type description: \"An electromagnetic water meter\". The wildcard note → footnotes and also maybe in description. I'll put the type designation wildcard explanation in description too? Footnotes entry covers it. I'll include footnote marker \"*\" and reference footnote_markers: [\"*\"] on type_designations? type_designations are plain strings; can't attach markers. I'll put the explanation in description.\n\nLet me write description: \"An electromagnetic water meter. Type designations use wildcards: X = 1 (standard), 3 (advanced) or 5 (premium, mobile Comms - MC) variant; Y = 1, 2, 8 or 9 (integral/remote version, optionally sensor only); Z = R (reduced bore), V (virtual full bore) or F (full bore).\"\n\nHmm, description should be the free-text description if present. I'll keep: \"An electromagnetic water meter\" and put wildcard info in footnotes. Maybe better include both. I'll include the full note in footnotes only, description = \"An electromagnetic water meter, Type: AquaMaster4 FEW4XY.Z and FET4*\".\n\nModel family models with attributes:\n[\n  {\"model_id\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"label\": \"AquaMaster4 FEW41Y.Z (standard variant, X=1)\", \"attributes\": {\"variant\": \"standard\"}},\n  {\"model_id\": \"FEW43Y.Z\", \"label\": \"AquaMaster4 FEW43Y.Z (advanced variant, X=3)\", \"attributes\": {\"variant\": \"advanced\"}},\n  {\"model_id\": \"FEW45Y.Z\", \"label\": \"AquaMaster4 FEW45Y.Z (premium / mobile Comms - MC variant, X=5)\", \"attributes\": {\"variant\": \"premium (mobile Comms - MC)\"}}\n]\n\nWait — is FEW41 = X=1 standard? The wildcard says X being 1 for standard, 3 for advanced, 5 for premium. FEW41Y.Z → X=1 → standard. FEW43 → advanced. FEW45 → premium MC. Reasonable inference, low risk. I'll include.\n\nShould I also include Y and Z axes as attributes? Y ∈ {1,2,8,9} integral/remote; Z ∈ {R,V,F} bore. I could add attributes: {\"y_options\": \"1, 2, 8, 9 (integral/remote version, optionally sensor only)\", \"z_options\": \"R (reduced bore), V (virtual full bore), F (full bore)\"}. Hmm — better at family level but schema has only family_name and models. I'll add these to each model's attributes? That's repetitive. Or skip; footnotes capture it. I'll skip but mention in footnote.\n\nAlso should model_family include FET4? The certified type includes FET4 transmitter. FET4* — with the same wildcard? Actually \"FET4 *\" where * refers to the footnote — hmm, FET4 is likely the transmitter (for remote/sensor-only versions). I'll leave it in type_designations.\n\nRecommendation accuracy_classes: [1, 2].\n\nCharacteristics: also \"flow_profile_sensitivity_class\" config:\n{\"attribute\": \"flow_profile_sensitivity_class\", \"axis\": \"bore size\", \"values\": [\n  {\"condition\": \"standard (0 x DN upstream and 0 x DN downstream)\", \"value\": \"U0 and D0\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"full bore sizes DN250 and larger (3 x DN upstream and 0 x DN downstream)\", \"value\": \"U3 and D0\"}\n]}\n\npressure_loss_class config:\n{\"attribute\": \"pressure_loss_class\", \"axis\": \"bore type and size\", \"values\": [\n  {\"condition\": \"reduced bore, DN40 and DN50\", \"value\": \"Δp 40 (0.40 bar)\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"reduced bore, sizes larger than DN50\", \"value\": \"Δp 63 (0.63 bar)\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"virtual or full bore, DN40 and DN50\", \"value\": \"Δp 10 (0.10 bar)\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"virtual or full bore, DN65 to DN200\", \"value\": \"Δp 16 (0.16 bar)\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"virtual or full bore, DN250 and larger\", \"value\": \"Δp 10 (0.10 bar)\"}\n]}\n\nValues as strings since they're class designations with pressure in parens.\n\nElectromagnetic environment model_level — decided:\nmodel_level entry 1: {\"attribute\": \"electromagnetic_environment\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"value\": \"E2\"}, {\"model\": \"FEW43Y.Z\", \"value\": \"E2\"}]}\nconfig entry for FEW45.\n\nBattery:\nmodel_level: {\"attribute\": \"replaceable_battery_cells\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"value\": 2}, {\"model\": \"FEW43Y.Z\", \"value\": 2}, {\"model\": \"FEW45Y.Z\", \"value\": 6}], \"unit_symbol\": \"x 3.6 V cells\"} — hmm unit_symbol should be a unit. Use \"cells\". And type-level battery_cell_voltage 3.6 V.\n\nActually \"2x 3,6 V\" means 2 cells of 3.6 V each. OK.\n\nAlso FEW45 backup batteries: config_level:\n{\"attribute\": \"backup_replaceable_battery_cells\", \"axis\": \"power source (FEW45Y.Z)\", \"values\": [\n  {\"condition\": \"AC mains\", \"value\": 4, \"unit_symbol\": \"cells\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"renewable energy power (DC powered)\", \"value\": 4, \"unit_symbol\": \"cells\"}\n]}\nHmm, unit_symbol \"cells\" isn't a unit but fine? Or omit unit_symbol. I'll omit.\n\nDo I want this much detail? It's faithful. Keep.\n\nNow software identification: \"See details in table 3\" / \"table 4\" — pointer, skip.\n\nChecking facilities: Type P.\n\nLet me also consider whether to include \"water_meter\" attributes like reverse_flow. Fine.\n\nShould characteristics.model_level include attributes per model from the tables? Tables 1 and 2 are identical except EMC and power supply bits. So model_level: electromagnetic_environment, replaceable_battery_cells (and backup batteries). Good.\n\nNow assembling JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"project_number\": \"3903947\",\n    \"page_total\": 13,\n    \"member_state\": \"The Netherlands\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2025-04-07\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"NMi Certin B.V.\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Thijsseweg 11\", \"2629 JA Delft\", \"The Netherlands\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"M.Ph.D. Schmidt\",\n    \"phone\": \"+31 88 636 2332\",\n    \"email\": \"certin@nmi.nl\",\n    \"website\": \"www.nmi.nl\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\"name\": \"ABB Limited\", \"address_lines\": [\"Oldends Lane\", \"GL10 3TA Stonehouse\", \"United Kingdom\"]}\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\"name\": \"ABB Limited\", \"address_lines\": [\"Oldends Lane\", \"GL10 3TA Stonehouse\", \"United Kingdom\"]}\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"AquaMaster4 FEW4XY.Z\", \"AquaMaster4 FET4*\"],\n    \"module_designation\": null,\n    \"description\": \"An electromagnetic water meter. Type designation wildcards: X = 1 (standard), 3 (advanced) or 5 (premium, mobile Comms - MC) variant; Y = 1, 2, 8 or 9 (integral/remote version, optionally sensor only); Z = R (reduced bore), V (virtual full bore) or F (full bore).\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": \"AquaMaster4\",\n    \"models\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"label\": \"AquaMaster4 FEW41Y.Z\", \"attributes\": {\"variant\": \"standard (X=1)\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"FEW43Y.Z\", \"label\": \"AquaMaster4 FEW43Y.Z\", \"attributes\": {\"variant\": \"advanced (X=3)\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"FEW45Y.Z\", \"label\": \"AquaMaster4 FEW45Y.Z\", \"attributes\": {\"variant\": \"premium (mobile Comms - MC) (X=5)\"}}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {\n      \"measuring_principle\": {\"value\": \"Electromagnetic\"},\n      \"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": \"1 and 2\"},\n      \"environmental_class\": {\"value\": \"O (installed outdoors)\"},\n      \"mechanical_class\": {\"value\": \"M1\"},\n      \"temperature_range_ambient\": {\"value\": {\"min\": -25, \"max\": 55}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n      \"water_temperature_class\": {\"value\": \"T50\"},\n      \"water_temperature_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 50}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n      \"maximum_admissible_pressure\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"MPa\"},\n      \"orientation\": {\"value\": \"All positions (horizontal, vertical, or diagonal)\"},\n      \"reverse_flow\": {\"value\": \"The sensor is intended to measure reverse flow\"},\n      \"checking_facilities\": {\"value\": \"Type P (permanent) automatic checking facility\"},\n      \"battery_cell_voltage\": {\"value\": 3.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n      \"battery_operating_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 2.9, \"max\": 3.6}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}\n    },\n    \"model_level\": [\n      {\"attribute\": \"electromagnetic_environment\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"value\": \"E2\"}, {\"model\": \"FEW43Y.Z\", \"value\": \"E2\"}]},\n      {\"attribute\": \"replaceable_battery_cells\", \"unit_symbol\": \"cells\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"value\": 2}, {\"model\": \"FEW43Y.Z\", \"value\": 2}, {\"model\": \"FEW45Y.Z\", \"value\": 6}]}\n    ],\n    \"config_level\": [\n      {\"attribute\": \"electromagnetic_environment\", \"axis\": \"external antenna cable (FEW45Y.Z)\", \"values\": [{\"condition\": \"with external antenna cable\", \"value\": \"E1\"}, {\"condition\": \"without external antenna cable\", \"value\": \"E2\"}]},\n      {\"attribute\": \"pressure_loss_class\", \"axis\": \"bore type and size\", \"values\": [...]},\n      {\"attribute\": \"flow_profile_sensitivity_class\", \"axis\": \"bore size\", \"values\": [...]},\n      {\"attribute\": \"power_supply_voltage\", \"axis\": \"power source\", \"values\": [\n        {\"condition\": \"AC mains\", \"value\": {\"min\": 95, \"max\": 240}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n        {\"condition\": \"renewable energy power (DC powered)\", \"value\": {\"min\": 6, \"max\": 32}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}\n      ]},\n      {\"attribute\": \"power_supply_frequency\", \"axis\": \"power source\", \"values\": [{\"condition\": \"AC mains\", \"value\": {\"min\": 50, \"max\": 60}, \"unit_symbol\": \"Hz\"}]},\n      {\"attribute\": \"backup_replaceable_battery_cells\", \"axis\": \"power source (FEW45Y.Z)\", \"values\": [{\"condition\": \"AC mains\", \"value\": 4}, {\"condition\": \"renewable energy power (DC powered)\", \"value\": 4}]}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R49-1\",\n    \"edition\": 2013,\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [1, 2]\n  },\n  \"test_reports\": [\n    {\"id\": \"NMi-2254799-01\", \"date\": \"2020-08-14\", \"pages\": 235, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NMi-2254799-03\", \"date\": \"2020-09-30\", \"pages\": 44, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NMi-2254799-04\", \"date\": \"2020-12-24\", \"pages\": 180, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NMi-2564429-01\", \"date\": \"2021-08-02\", \"pages\": 26, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NMi-2496280-01\", \"date\": \"2021-08-26\", \"pages\": 29, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NMi-2496280-02\", \"date\": \"2021-11-23\", \"pages\": 25, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NMi-2563125-01\", \"date\": \"2023-09-22\", \"pages\": 94, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n    {\"id\": \"T11851-9\", \"role\": \"documentation_file\"}\n  ],\n  \"revision_history\": [\n    {\"revision\": \"12\", \"date\": \"2025-04-07\"}\n  ],\n  \"footnotes\": [\n    {\"marker\": \"*\", \"text\": \"With X being 1 for standard or 3 for advanced or 5 for premium (mobile Comms - MC) variant; Y being 1, 2, 8 or 9 (integral/remote version, optionally sensor only); Z being R (reduced bore), V (virtual full bore) or F (full bore).\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nCheck: temperature range \"T50 (+0,1 °C / +50 °C)\" → min 0.1, max 50. Good, decimal comma fixed.\n\nMAP \"1,6 MPa (16 bar)\" → 1.6 MPa. Good.\n\n\"95 –240 VAC @ 50/60 Hz\" → 95-240 V, 50-60 Hz. Good.\n\nBattery \"2x 3,6 V (operating range: 2,9 - 3,6 V)\" → cells 2, cell voltage 3.6 V, operating range 2.9-3.6 V. Good.\n\nΔ character — Unicode fine, not LaTeX. OK. Maybe write \"Δp 40 (0.40 bar)\".\n\nOne concern: model_level values shape per schema: \"values[]: {model, value, footnote_markers[]}\" — value objects like {\"model\": \"FEW41Y.Z\", \"value\": \"E2\"} — fine. Unit for attribute-level (unit_symbol on the model_level entry) — example in R137 shows unit_symbol at attribute level. Good, I did that for replaceable_battery_cells.\n\nconfig_level values: {condition, value, unit_symbol}. Good.\n\nDo I include \"module_designation\": null? Schema lists it; certified_type module_designation for R49 water meter — \"Not applicable\" probably. I'll set null... or omit. Rules say omit if not present. I'll omit. Hmm, schema shows it as a field with null option. I'll include \"module_designation\": null? Actually a water meter under R49 isn't a module-based cert; safest: omit. I'll omit.\n\nAlso certificate \"scheme\": \"A\" — from \"issued under scheme A\". Good.\n\nrevision_history changes: omit.\n\nDate format: ISO. Good.\n\nOne more check — \"Person responsible: M.Ph.D. Schmidt\" — include as person_responsible. Title unknown — the word before address \"Certification Board\" — I'll leave omitted.\n\nPage 1: \"Issuing Authority: NMi Certin B.V., OIML Issuing Authority NL1\" — name could include \", OIML Issuing Authority NL1\". I'll keep name \"NMi Certin B.V.\" and oiml_issuer_id \"NL1\".\n\nTest report dates: \"2 August 2021\" → 2021-08-02 ✓.\n\nI think the JSON is ready. Output single JSON object, no fences.",
      "signature": "053b6481a2c74d29a7daefb5"
    },
